<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. Augustine, Florida</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1565">1565</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">St. Augustine is a city on the Atlantic coast of north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, founded in 1565 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-menendez-de-aviles">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés</a>, who went on to destroy the French Huguenot colony at Fort Caroline. As capital of Spanish Florida, defended by the stone <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castillo-de-san-marcos">Castillo de San Marcos</a>, it relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and labour from the Apalachee and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timucua">Timucua</a> missions. It is the oldest continuously inhabited European-founded city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/st-augustine-florida.jpg" alt="St. Augustine, Florida" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schwerdf · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_the_Castillo_de_San_Marcos,_St._Augustine,_FL_2025-05-20.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
